The Noto family of fonts is one of the largest undertakings in the
history of type founding. It certainly has not been a straight line from
point A to B\@. I've been involved on and off for 14 years, and there are
about 60 others who have contributed to it up to this day. This doesn't
include the efforts on the Chinese, Japanese and Korean fonts, which
people from Adobe would have to tell you about.

